from release_tools import package
package('V1.14.0','''# V1.14.0 — Linked Input Files and Rules Workflow

Enhances V1.13.0. Input Files now conditionally reveals Zip Folder Name when isZipFolder is checked. Zip Folder Name identifies the archive or archive pattern; Filename identifies the member to read inside it, including nested folders. Saved-path matching uses the archive name for ZIP inputs. The archive is read safely in memory without filesystem extraction and requires exactly one matching member of the selected type. Unsafe entries, oversized content and encrypted ZIPs remain rejected.

File Purpose, Type of File, Delimiter, Encoding, Filename and File Path are mandatory for new or edited definitions. ZIP inputs also require Zip Folder Name ending in .zip. The ZIP checkbox records Yes/No. Read Mode, watch interval, Max Columns, Header Row and Sheet Password are optional, with Manual/60 seconds/100 columns/row 1 defaults. Existing definitions remain readable until edited. In Excel settings, Has Sheet Password? Yes reveals password controls; No hides them and clears any saved secret. Passwords are encrypted with Windows DPAPI and never included in GitHub or configuration snapshots. Password-required encrypted Excel is supported; worksheet protection alone does not require a password to read. File reads stay inside Codex.

Samples are uploaded per input under Input Files and show only uploaded filename/status there. The legacy sample uploader also lives in that tab. No raw-data preview appears in Input Files or Retailer Details. Rules Configure has one Preview button opening a walkthrough with Previous/Next and a step selector: raw primary input, each ordered rule, linking, Layout Rules and final Column Mapping. Before/After tables show at most 25 rows and validation findings show their rule step. Final sample CSV export remains inside this preview. Actual weekly KPI evaluation runs during batch processing, rather than sample preview.

Rules Configure offers Cleaning, Transformation, Validation, Link Files and KPI components. It retains individual ordered rows, descriptions, fixed 909/908 execution messages, description editing, settings/Condition editing, custom rule definitions and the complete reference catalogue. Input-stage rules can target individual files. Link Files offers dropdowns for left/right files, matching columns and Inner/Left/Right/Full Outer/Cross join types. Subsequent links can use the current linked result as their left input. Matching compares trimmed, case-sensitive textual keys; blank keys never match, and duplicate keys expand matches. Colliding right columns receive the configured prefix; remaining collisions are rejected. Cross joins combine every row pair. Linked output is bounded to 100,000 rows.

Layout Rules adds Cleaning, Transformation and Validation rules operating on the combined result after linking. Invalid layout order and unavailable matching/mapping fields are rejected. A Primary Input selection identifies the file that starts linked processing and supplies the preview's primary sample. Every participating sample must be current for previews. During batch launch, the primary upload/saved-path file and all rule-targeted companion inputs are parsed and captured privately before execution. Companions require exactly one file matching their saved path/name. Input settings or setup changes during capture trigger a retry request. Later file edits cannot change an accepted run. Reprocessing reads current companions and uses current configuration. Automatic reading starts linked jobs only from the configured primary input, while the app runs; companions are read when that job starts. Start a linked Data Streams upload with its saved primary Input File Settings. Linked input metadata records filenames, received row counts, sizes and content hashes, without displaying cleaned data in audits. The temporary dataset cache is removed on completion/cancellation.

Column Mapping is a separate Rules Configure tab controlling included source columns, output names and column order. An empty mapping retains all columns; a populated mapping defines the complete output selection. Output Format is a separate tab with dropdown-selected analytics columns, saved against the final output names. Analytics execution is reserved for a future version; this selection does not change the output file format. Mapping and analytics selections are versioned in configuration history and captured per job. Column mapping is applied after the rules and recorded in the audit; output column order is preserved in API previews and CSV exports.

KPI Checks has moved out of Input Files into an explicitly added KPI rule for a Transaction input. Put this rule last and choose the final mapped Sales, Quantity and Store ID names. Its default ranges and lookback remain ±30% store / ±30% retailer / ±40% count, previous 8 weeks. KPI evaluation uses final mapped output after all rules. A run without a KPI rule does not perform KPI checks; older input-profile KPI settings no longer enable checks automatically. Historical KPI snapshots and review/approval timestamps remain available. Flagged KPI runs still finish Completed with Interruption and require a recorded manual check before approval. Execution failures still retry three times and retain a cancelled batch log with failure details.

The single outputs/V1.3.A1.bat launcher opens V1.14.0 at http://127.0.0.1:5001/. Close the old server window and reopen this launcher after updating. Local SQLite data is preserved using backup. Databases, uploads, samples, encrypted secrets, personal configuration, dependencies and generated builds are excluded from GitHub.
''','''Production Vite build and 130 backend tests passed. Fourteen linked-workflow tests cover all five joins, duplicate/blank/trimmed/case-sensitive keys, output bounds and collision errors, ZIP archive-name scoping and named nested-member selection, mandatory fields and optional defaults, conditional password storage/clearing, legacy pre-link rules, ordered sample walkthroughs and CSV columns, linked/Layout rules and analytics selections, invalid sequence and stale samples, mapping validation, captured companion content, raw-data privacy in audits, unavailable companions, primary-input enforcement, referenced-input deletion protection, empty inner joins, and three-attempt validation cancellation. Existing 116 tests cover KPI review/approval, parsing/passwords, archive, history, audit, stores, readiness, comparison and served frontend assets. Interactive browser verification was not performed.
''',launcher=True)
